From 1dba7d23863eb0d4739a7ec0d01bdf4954517f10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lolzen <funer@gmx.at>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 10:15:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: Switch the Wi-Fi backend with runit when booted with it

The backend switch stopped and started NetworkManager and the backends
through org.freedesktop.systemd1 only. It now uses the init system's
services, as fan control does.

runit has two gaps that systemd covers: a backend that dbus-daemon
started for NetworkManager is not a runit service, and a backend that
D-Bus cannot activate is not started by anything (Void ships iwd without
an activation file). On runit the old backend is therefore terminated
through its bus name, and the new backend's runit service is enabled
when D-Bus cannot activate it. systemd systems are unchanged.
